# Koka 3.0.x Released { .heading-no-number }

~ begin blog-meta
**January 2024** · Language, Release
~ end blog-meta

---

The Koka 3.0.x series introduces experimental support for implicit parameters and locally qualified names, alongside major improvements to the VS Code integration.

---

## Implicit Parameters

Koka 3.0.1 introduces **implicit parameters**, an experimental feature that allows for parameterized overloading of operations like equality and show.

## Locally Qualified Names

This release introduces **locally qualified names**, always enabling references to (overloaded) identifiers explicitly. This helps resolve ambiguities without full qualification.

## VS Code Integration

Major improvements have landed for the VS Code integration:
- **Inlay Hints**: Press and hold `ctrl+alt` (or `ctrl+option` on macOS) to show inferred types, fully qualified names, and implicit arguments.
- **Revised Hover Information**: Improved hover and inlay information for better developer productivity.

## Standard Library Refinement

In v3.0.4, `std/core` has been revised and split into separate modules for better organization and maintenance.

